description:
## Summary

On component pages, the **Variation Showcase** (kitchen-sink) block renders a static screenshot followed by **Live Core App** / **Live Express App** buttons. The screenshot itself was not clickable.

This wraps the screenshot in a link to the Express shinylive app, so clicking the preview image opens the live app — matching the intuition that the preview is interactive. It also adds a hover affordance: the image dims to `0.7` opacity on hover (using the same `0.15s ease-in-out` timing as the buttons) to signal it's clickable.

## Change

Shared partial used by every component page (`components/_partials/components-detail-kitchen-sink.ejs`):

```diff
-![](<%= item.image %>){.border .my-4 style="border-radius: .5em;"}
+[![](<%= item.image %>){.border .my-4 style="border-radius: .5em;"}](<%= item.express %>){target="_blank"}
```

Plus a hover style in `quarto-style.scss`:

```scss
.kitchensink a > img {
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: opacity 0.15s ease-in-out;
}

.kitchensink a > img:hover {
  opacity: 0.7;
}
```

Targeting `item.express` per the issue title. The two existing buttons still provide both Core and Express links.

## Demo

Hovering the Showcase image on the deploy preview (dims to `0.7`):

![Hovering the Variation Showcase image dims it to signal it is a link](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/posit-dev/py-shiny-site/748b749d4970bae3ef78042ee92291b39ffac0a7/kitchen-sink-hover.gif)

## Scope

This partial is shared by all component pages (~40), so it's a site-wide affordance improvement.

